    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "The shared envelope",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "targets": [

      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
        },
        "overrides": [

        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**rio is a single node with local-path PVCs.** This node disk is the\n**physical pool every PVC below carves from.** local-path has **no\nper-volume quota** — so a full node disk wedges **ALL PVCs at once**.\nThe root `/` (ext4, `/dev/nvme1n1p2`) is the data envelope; the zfs\npools (`/srv/pool/*`, `/var/lib/k3s-storage`) are the host’s bulk\nstorage. Watch *this* row for the truth — the PVC row below is\nmisleading on local-path (it reads this same whole-node fs).\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Filesystem used % (by mount) — the real fs",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
