        "content": "**This is the REAL postgres footprint** — `cnpg_pg_database_size_bytes`,\nthe actual per-database size reported by CloudNativePG. It is what\n*actually* consumes the node disk, vs the misleading local-path PVC\nstats above (which all read the whole node fs). When you ask “how\nmuch storage is postgres using?”, **this row is the answer**, not the\nPVC row. (Two pods — the CNPG HA pair `pangea-database-1/-2` — so the\nqueries `max by(datname)` to dedupe the replicas.)\n"
      }
