    {
      "id": 27,
      "title": "Why storage carving is parked on local-path",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 90
      },
      "targets": [

      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
        },
        "overrides": [

        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**breathe carves storage by growing `spec.storage.size` before a\nvolume fills** — BUT on local-path the per-volume metric is\n**unrepresentable**: `kubelet_volume_stats` reports the\n**whole-node-fs**, so every storage band reads the *same* `used`\n(≈459 GB on rio for authentik-postgresql / garage-data /\npangea-database alike). With no per-volume signal, the storage\nbands sit **MetricUnrepresentable / Conflict and DON’T carve** —\nall are `dry_run=1` (SHADOW), and `nats-jetstream` produces no\n`util_ratio` at all. (The util that *does* appear is on a 0–100\nscale while `setpoint_ratio`=0.8 / `grow_above_ratio`=0.85 are\n0–1 — the scale mismatch is itself part of the unrepresentable\nstate.) **Storage carving goes live on a CSI with per-volume\naccounting (Longhorn / Ceph / EBS).** The\n`cnpg_pg_database_size_bytes` above is what breathe *would* carve\nagainst if it could see per-volume.\n"
      }
    },
